---
import BroadcastStage from '../components/studio/BroadcastStage.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import PostHog from '../components/posthog.astro';
import { createPlaybackUrl } from '../lib/player/PlaybackLink';
import type { Experience } from '../lib/models/Experience';
import forest from '../data/experiences/forest.json';
import temple from '../data/experiences/temple.json';
import ocean from '../data/experiences/ocean.json';

const scenes = [forest, temple, ocean].map(scene => ({
  name: scene.name,
  id: scene.id,
  image: `/images/experience-covers/${scene.id}.jpg`,
  playback: createPlaybackUrl(scene as Experience, ''),
}));
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Design a distinctive setting for your video podcast in OBS. Personalise your show title, camera layout, names, colour, logo and subtle background motion with Aether." />
    <title>Podcast backdrops and show design for OBS — Aether</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <PostHog />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Aether home"><img src="/brand/aether-mark.svg" alt="" width="52" height="52" /><span>Aether</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="/studio/podcast/">Podcast Studio →</a></nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Aether for podcasts and streams</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">A setting for<br />your video podcast.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Give your show a distinctive look. Personalise your title, camera layout, names and colour, add your logo, and choose subtle background motion. Bring your setting into OBS for your next recording or stream.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/studio/podcast/">Personalise your show →</a><a class="button secondary" href="#show-preview">See a show layout</a></div>
        <p class="hero-note">One host or two people · Your show branding · Silent visuals for OBS</p>
      </section>

      <figure class="show-demo">
        <img src="/images/podcast/aether-podcast-demo.webp" alt="Illustrative two-person podcast composition with fictional presenters, gold camera frames and The Evening Conversation branding against a Liverpool waterfront setting." width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>Illustrative demo with AI-generated presenters. This still mockup shows the concept; the interactive preview below uses the actual Aether player.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section id="show-preview" class="preview-section" aria-labelledby="show-preview-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your show, in context</p><h2 id="show-preview-title">Picture your next episode.</h2></div><p>A reusable setting with a show title, camera frames and names. Try the layouts below, then personalise your own in Podcast Studio.</p></div>
        <BroadcastStage />
        <div class="preview-controls">
          <div class="scene-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Choose an example camera layout">
            <button type="button" class="scene-button show-layout" data-layout="solo" aria-pressed="false">One host</button>
            <button type="button" class="scene-button show-layout" data-layout="duo" aria-pressed="true">Two people</button>
            <button type="button" class="scene-button show-layout" data-layout="background" aria-pressed="false">No frames</button>
          </div>
          <button type="button" id="show-motion" class="button secondary" aria-pressed="false">Play subtle motion</button>
        </div>
        <p class="caption">Illustrative layout with camera placeholders. Add your real cameras and microphone in OBS. This example uses the Liverpool setting; motion is silent and respects your device’s reduced-motion preference.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="backdrop-preview" class="preview-section" aria-labelledby="preview-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Explore the ambience tools</p><h2 id="preview-title">Explore more backdrops.</h2></div><p>These separate ambience scenes show Aether’s adjustable environments. They are backdrop-only previews; the Podcast Studio above adds show branding and camera layouts.</p></div>
        <div class="preview-frame">
          <img id="scene-poster" src={scenes[0].image} alt="Forest backdrop: a woodland clearing at dusk" width="1920" height="1080" />
          <iframe id="scene-player" title="Silent Forest backdrop preview" hidden loading="lazy"></iframe>
        </div>
        <div class="preview-controls">
          <div class="scene-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Choose a backdrop preview">
            {scenes.map((scene, i) => <button type="button" class="scene-button" data-name={scene.name} data-image={scene.image} data-playback={scene.playback} aria-pressed={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}>{scene.name}</button>)}
          </div>
          <button type="button" id="preview-toggle" class="button secondary" aria-controls="scene-player" aria-pressed="false">Play silent preview</button>
        </div>
        <p class="caption">Live Aether visuals, rendered in your browser. No camera is included in this preview.</p>
        <noscript><p>Open Studio to customise your setting and use it in OBS.</p></noscript>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="make-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your scene, your style</p><h2 id="make-title">Give your content a setting.</h2></div><p>Keep a consistent setting across episodes. Podcast Studio brings your show identity and camera layout together around a gently animated backdrop.</p></div>
        <div class="card-grid">
          <article class="card"><h3>Choose your layout</h3><p>Use one host, two people or no frames. Preview where your cameras will sit before composing the recording in OBS.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Make the show yours</h3><p>Add your show title, episode text and participant names. Set your accent colour and upload your logo; use the downloaded OBS file to include it.</p></article>
          <article class="card"><h3>Set the motion</h3><p>Choose Still, Subtle or Atmospheric. Keep movement restrained for conversation, with silent output that leaves your audio setup to OBS.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="how-it-works" class="section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">From Studio to recording</p><h2 id="workflow-title">Personalise. Export. Record.</h2></div><p>Design your show setting in Aether. Add cameras and a microphone in OBS to record or stream.</p></div>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Personalise your show</h3><p>Open Podcast Studio. Choose a layout, enter your show details, set your colour and motion, and optionally add a logo.</p></li>
          <li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Keep your setting</h3><p>Changes are saved automatically in this browser on this device. Download your OBS file to keep an exported copy of the current setting.</p></li>
          <li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Select Add to OBS</h3><p>Follow the setup instructions to copy your OBS link or download an HTML file. Use the file if you have added a logo.</p></li>
          <li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3>Add your camera</h3><p>Add the backdrop as a Browser source in OBS at 1920 × 1080. Place your camera sources above it and fit them inside the frames. Record or stream using your usual microphone setup.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="section questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Before you record</p><h2 id="questions-title">A few useful details.</h2>
        <details><summary>How does the backdrop appear behind me?</summary><p>In OBS, place your camera source above the Aether Browser source. A camera inset keeps your room visible inside that inset. To appear directly within the environment, use a green screen with chroma key or a separate camera background removal tool. Aether creates the environment; your recording setup handles the camera.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Will the backdrop play sound over my microphone?</summary><p>No. Podcast Studio exports silent visuals. Manage your microphone and any other audio in OBS.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is the difference between a link and an HTML file?</summary><p>The link includes your show text, layout, colour and motion: leave Local File unticked in OBS and paste it. To include an uploaded logo, download the HTML file, tick Local File and select it. Both need an internet connection to load the Aether player.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do edits automatically update my OBS backdrop?</summary><p>The export contains the settings you chose at that moment. After making changes, select Add to OBS again and copy a new link or download a new file. Replace the previous export in your OBS Browser source.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is this a downloadable video?</summary><p>It is a browser-rendered backdrop with animated effects. OBS can record it as part of your finished video or use it in a live stream.</p></details>
      </section>

      <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="start-title"><p class="eyebrow">Make your first backdrop</p><h2 id="start-title">Give your next episode<br />a setting of its own.</h2><a class="button primary" href="/studio/podcast/">Personalise your show →</a></section>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
    <script>
      import { createBroadcastController } from '../lib/broadcast/BroadcastController';
      import { defaultBroadcast } from '../lib/broadcast/BroadcastSettings';
      const showRoot = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#show-preview .broadcast-stage')!;
      const showController = createBroadcastController(showRoot);
      const layoutButtons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.show-layout');
      const motionButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#show-motion')!;
      let showSettings = { ...defaultBroadcast, motion: 'still' as const };
      let showPlaying = false;
      function renderShow() {
        showController.update({ ...showSettings, motion: showPlaying ? 'subtle' : 'still' }, '', true);
        layoutButtons.forEach(button => button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button.dataset.layout === showSettings.layout)));
        motionButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(showPlaying));
        motionButton.textContent = showPlaying ? 'Stop motion' : 'Play subtle motion';
      }
      layoutButtons.forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const layout = button.dataset.layout;
        if (layout === 'solo' || layout === 'duo' || layout === 'background') {
          showSettings = { ...showSettings, layout }; renderShow();
        }
      }));
      motionButton.addEventListener('click', () => { showPlaying = !showPlaying; renderShow(); });
      renderShow();
      window.addEventListener('pagehide', event => { if (!event.persisted) showController.destroy(); });
      const poster = document.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>('#scene-poster')!;
      const player = document.querySelector<HTMLIFrameElement>('#scene-player')!;
      const toggle = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#preview-toggle')!;
      const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('#backdrop-preview .scene-button');
      let selected = buttons[0];
      let playing = false;
      function render() {
        poster.src = selected.dataset.image!;
        poster.alt = `${selected.dataset.name} backdrop scene`;
        player.title = `Silent ${selected.dataset.name} backdrop preview`;
        player.hidden = !playing;
        poster.hidden = playing;
        if (playing) player.src = selected.dataset.playback!;
        else player.removeAttribute('src');
        toggle.textContent = playing ? 'Stop preview' : 'Play silent preview';
        toggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(playing));
        buttons.forEach(button => button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button === selected)));
      }
      buttons.forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => { selected = button; render(); }));
      toggle.addEventListener('click', () => { playing = !playing; render(); });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
<style>
  :global(body) { margin:0; min-width:320px; font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif; color:#f4efe7; background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 80% 0%,#24203980,transparent 45%),#090b0f; }
  * { box-sizing:border-box; }
  a { color:inherit; text-decoration:none; }
  button { font:inherit; cursor:pointer; }
  a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible { outline:3px solid #66e3ff; outline-offset:5px; }
  [hidden] { display:none!important; }
  main,.site-header { width:min(1180px,calc(100% - 40px)); margin:auto; }
  .site-header { padding:28px 0; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:24px; }
  .brand { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.08em; }
  nav { display:flex; gap:24px; flex-wrap:wrap; color:#b8bdc8; font-size:.9rem; }
  nav a:hover { color:#66e3ff; }
  .skip-link { position:absolute; left:20px; top:-80px; z-index:10; background:#fff; color:#090b0f; padding:12px; }
  .skip-link:focus { top:12px; }
  .hero { padding:90px 0 70px; max-width:930px; }
  .eyebrow { color:#b2a5ff; font-size:.78rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.13em; text-transform:uppercase; margin:0 0 22px; }
  h1 { margin:0; font-size:clamp(3.7rem,8vw,7.2rem); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.06em; }
  .lead { max-width:730px; color:#b4b8c3; font-size:clamp(1.1rem,2vw,1.35rem); line-height:1.75; margin:30px 0; }
  .actions { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:14px; }
  .button { min-height:48px; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:12px 23px; border-radius:999px; border:1px solid #ffffff30; font-weight:650; }
  .primary { background:#f4efe7; color:#090b0f; }
  .secondary { color:#f4efe7; background:#ffffff08; }
  .button:hover { border-color:#66e3ff; }
  .hero-note,.caption { color:#9fa6b5; line-height:1.7; font-size:.9rem; }
  .hero-note { margin-top:24px; }
  .show-demo { margin:0 0 32px; }
  .show-demo img { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; border:1px solid #ffffff25; border-radius:20px; }
  .show-demo figcaption { margin-top:14px; color:#9fa6b5; font-size:.9rem; line-height:1.7; }
  .preview-section,.section { padding:70px 0; border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff1a; }
  .section-heading { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr; align-items:end; gap:70px; margin-bottom:36px; }
  h2 { margin:0; font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3.7rem); letter-spacing:-.045em; line-height:1.1; }
  .section-heading>p,.card p,.steps p,details p { color:#b4b8c3; line-height:1.75; }
  .section-heading>p { margin:0; }
  .preview-frame { aspect-ratio:16/9; position:relative; border:1px solid #ffffff25; border-radius:20px; overflow:hidden; background:#000; }
  .preview-frame img,.preview-frame iframe { width:100%; height:100%; display:block; object-fit:cover; border:0; }
  .preview-controls { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:20px; flex-wrap:wrap; padding-top:20px; }
  .scene-buttons { display:flex; gap:8px; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  .scene-button { color:#b4b8c3; background:#111722; border:1px solid #ffffff25; border-radius:999px; padding:12px 20px; }
  .scene-button[aria-pressed="true"] { color:#cff9e4; background:#163c2c; border-color:#67df9f; }
  .card-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:18px; }
  .card,.steps li { padding:28px; background:#ffffff06; border:1px solid #ffffff1a; border-radius:20px; }
  h3 { font-size:1.3rem; margin:0 0 16px; letter-spacing:-.02em; }
  .card p,.steps p { margin:0; }
  .steps { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:18px; padding:0; margin:0; list-style:none; }
  .step-number { display:block; color:#66e3ff; font-size:.8rem; letter-spacing:.1em; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:30px; }
  .questions h2 { margin-bottom:32px; }
  details { border-top:1px solid #ffffff1a; padding:22px 0; }
  summary { cursor:pointer; font-weight:650; font-size:1.05rem; }
  details p { max-width:850px; margin-bottom:0; }
  .closing { padding:90px 0 20px; }
  .closing .button { margin-top:32px; }
  @media(max-width:750px) { .section-heading,.card-grid,.steps { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:20px; } .site-header { align-items:flex-start; } nav { gap:14px; justify-content:flex-end; } .hero { padding:60px 0 40px; } .section,.preview-section { padding:50px 0; } }
  @media(max-width:440px) { main,.site-header { width:calc(100% - 32px); } nav a[href="#how-it-works"] { display:none; } .brand img { width:40px; height:40px; } h1 { font-size:3.5rem; } .preview-controls { gap:16px; } .scene-button { padding:10px 16px; } .card,.steps li { padding:24px; } }
</style>
